## HOW A FROZEN TEXT IS READ
Every text stands in a fenced block whose first line is `[[TEXT <id>]]`; the text is every line after the id line up to the closing fence, joined by line feeds, no line feed at its end. Its length and sha256 (UTF-8, unfilled) are in THE FROZEN TABLE; **check every one BEFORE filling; a difference is a STOP.** Fill-ins are `<<NAME>>`, replaced by program only; **no `<<` may remain in anything you write.** `<<WRITE-DATE>>` is `date +%Y-%m-%d` at the write; `<<HHMM>>` the clock of the history write from `date`, once, as `HH:MM`. The seven owed numbers, in this order, are the highest owed number of the live `BACKLOG.md` plus 1 to plus 7: `<<OWED-NONELEM>>`, `<<OWED-HOSTCHAR>>`, `<<OWED-DIRPERM>>`, `<<OWED-NONASCII>>`, `<<OWED-UTF16>>`, `<<OWED-R2CELLS>>`, `<<OWED-FIRSTRUN>>` (106 to 112 at drafting; PREDICTED). The C-numbers are P-7's. `<<MAIN-SHORT>>`, `<<ORIGIN-CLOCK>>`, `<<PR-TOTAL>>`, `<<PR-OPEN>>` are THE ORIGIN's. `<<TICKED>>` is the owed numbers of slot TICKS joined as English (`98, 99, 100, 101 and 102`), `<<TICK-COUNT>>` their count as a word (`five`). `<<JIRA-COUNT>>` is the count of issues this pass CREATED as a numeral, or `no` when it created none; `<<JIRA-CREATED>>` is `<n> tickets created, one per item: ` followed by `<label> <key>` for each create in T-order, joined by `, ` (labels: THE JIRA TABLE's last column), or `no ticket created`; `<<JIRA-SKIPPED>>` is `No create was skipped: before each create a search for its summary found no issue holding it` or `Skipped as already present (an issue holding the same summary): ` followed by `<label> <key>` for each skip, joined by `, `. Slot JIRA HOLD uses H-JIRA-HOLD in place of H-JIRA, and `<<JIRA-COUNT>>` is `no`. **This kit holds no text alone: a text that fails a check STOPS its step whole** (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <text id> <check>`).

