## PART 4: THE JIRA CREATES (slot JIRA WRITE; the SECOND write of Step 4, after `CLARIFICATIONS.md`, before `BACKLOG.md`)
**The one shape of every create** (your helper builds it from THE JIRA TABLE and the frozen texts; THE JIRA FENCE refuses any other): `POST /rest/api/3/issue` with the JSON body
`{"fields": {"project": {"key": "OXPD2"}, "issuetype": {"id": "10030"}, "summary": <J-S text>, "description": <ADF of the J-D text>, "assignee": {"accountId": "626881c70f0cc0006f8ee5c9"}, "duedate": "2026-12-08", "labels": ["oxpd-workpath-question"]}, "update": {"issuelinks": [{"add": {"type": {"id": "10003"}, "outwardIssue": {"key": "OXPD2-1"}}}]}}`
**The ADF of a J-D text** (by program, never by hand): split the text on `\n\n` into blocks; a block whose every line starts with `>` is ONE `blockquote` node whose `paragraph` children are its lines split on lines equal to `>`, each line with its leading `> ` removed (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER: every quoted group is one line); any other block is ONE `paragraph` node holding ONE `text` node with the block's text (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER: every such block is one line). No marks, no other node. **The inverse** (for the read-back): a `paragraph` gives its text nodes joined; a `blockquote` gives `> ` plus each child paragraph's text, joined by `\n>\n`; nodes are joined by `\n\n`; any other node type is UNEQUAL. The drafter's round trip gave each of the 29 J-D texts back byte for byte (THE DRY-RUN FIGURES K7).
**THE SKIP RULE (idempotent by summary; before EVERY create, inside the same process):** (a) search `project = OXPD2 AND ( labels = "oxpd-workpath-question" )` and GET each hit's summary; (b) the project reader's phrase search for the J-S text (`text ~ "\"<summary>\""`, the reader softens it only on a non-200); (c) if any issue of (a) or (b) holds a summary EQUAL to the J-S text, byte for byte: SKIP this T-id, write `{"kind": "skip", "t": <T-id>, "key": <key>}` to the write log, create nothing; (d) if (b) returns a key that is neither equal nor one this pass created: `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY jira near-duplicate <T-id> <key>` (no create); (e) else create. **After a create:** HTTP 201 and a key `OXPD2-<n>`; write `{"kind": "create", "t": <T-id>, "key": <key>, "clock": <date>}` to the write log at once; then GET `issue/<key>?fields=summary,description,assignee,duedate,labels,issuelinks,issuetype,status,project` and check: summary EQUAL; the inverse of the description EQUAL to the J-D text; assignee account id `626881c70f0cc0006f8ee5c9`; duedate `2026-12-08`; labels exactly `["oxpd-workpath-question"]`; issue type id `10030`; project `OXPD2`; exactly one issue link, type `Relates`, to `OXPD2-1`; a one-character mutant of the summary UNEQUAL (control). Write `{"kind": "verify", ...}`. **Any answer but 201, a time-out, or a read-back that is not EQUAL: STOP at once** (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY jira <T-id> <what>`); after a non-201 or a time-out, run THE SKIP RULE's search (a) and (b) for that T-id FIRST and name what it found: a create may have landed without its answer. **Never retry a create blindly; never edit, delete or transition anything.** Space the creates at least 3.2 s apart (the project reader's own spacing for writes).
**THE JIRA FENCE (your helper refuses, by code, before any request leaves the process; each refusal is a selftest case that must fire):** any method but GET and POST; a POST to any path but `/rest/api/3/issue`; a body whose keys are not exactly `fields` and `update`, whose `fields` keys are not exactly the seven above, or any value outside the shape above; a T-id not in THE JIRA TABLE or already created or skipped in the write log; a create out of T-order; a 30th create; a summary or description not EQUAL to its frozen text (sha256 of the J-S and J-D texts against THE FROZEN TABLE); a text whose `scan_jira` codes differ from THE JIRA TABLE's codes column (a new code is a STOP; the codes that stand there are named in THE JIRA TEXT RULE); a text holding the value of any key of the project's `.env` (checked in-process, never printed; control: a planted value fires); the slot JIRA not WRITE; a file `.tools/b2030/HOLD` present; the clock at or after HARD STOP minus 10.
**THE JIRA TEXT RULE (the drafter's list over the project's own `scan_jira`; it is NOT the project's records rule).** The project's `scan_jira` (from `b1785.py`, loaded by `importlib`) is run on the summary and on each paragraph of the ADF; the codes it prints for each T-id must EQUAL THE JIRA TABLE's codes column. The codes that stand, and why each is accepted: `S-NAME` (the texts name the product owner as "Kam (product owner)" and quote his words, which name people: his instruction asks for exactly that); `S-DQUOTE` (his words and the pack's questions are quoted); `S-WORD:tuesday` (the weekday of the due date, "Tuesday 2026-12-08", not the coordinator); `S-WORD:lane` (T-26 only: "swim-lane" and "lanes:" in the diagram ask); `S-ASCII` (T-27 to T-29 only: the em dash U+2014 in his board words "b — Steve M's: ticket them", as the board's reader printed them). Never standing: `S-CARD`, `S-URL`, `S-BNUM`, `S-BTICK`, `S-NEWLINE`, `S-PLACEHOLDER`, and every `S-WORD` other than those two (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER: none of them fires on any of the 29).
**THE JIRA CORRECTIONS (the drafter's; each printed by its program, `jira_texts.py`; Q2):** (C1) T-27, T-28 and T-29 said "(tap at 10:34)" of his tap on the reporting card; the board reader prints that tap at `10:32:43` (the store's ruling time 10:35:06 is the coordinator's entry): each now says "(tap at 10:32)". (C2) T-29's "Why the build needs it: " was empty in the drafts file; the meeting pack gives W43's reason as "As the item above.", that is W42's: T-29 now carries T-28's reason, copied by program: "A customer's live rule may differ from the template, and the report rows have to match what those queries read." Nothing else of the drafts file is changed; the drafts' "First comment" paragraphs and the T-26 note for the seat are NOT written to Jira (this kit writes nothing to Jira but the creates; Q3).

